/// The City and County of San Francisco.
///
/// California cities do not tax income, so what San Francisco adds for its
/// residents is small. This system exists to show the last link of the chain
/// `us`, `us/ca`, `us/ca/san-francisco`: an entity that `lives` here is under
/// the city's laws, California's and the federal government's, all three.
///
/// One illustrative rule is written: the real property transfer tax, owed by
/// the seller on the price of a sale.
///
/// SAMPLE DATA. The rates are community-maintained and were written from the
/// published tax table, not checked against the Office of the Assessor-Recorder.
/// Verify them against the City (sfassessor.org, "Transfer tax") before relying
/// on them, and correct them in a pull request when they are wrong.
system us/ca/san-francisco

use us/ca


/// The City and County of San Francisco.
entity sf : government


/// Selling real property in San Francisco owes the city a transfer tax on the
/// price (Business and Tax Regulations Code, Article 12-C). The rate rises
/// with the price and applies to all of it, not only to the part above each
/// step. It is owed when the sale is recorded. Only sales up to 5,000,000 USD
/// are covered; above that the rates rise sharply, so work the tax out with
/// the Assessor-Recorder and record it by hand.
///
/// This is charged per lot sold, so a property held as several lots is taxed
/// lot by lot.
///
/// To fix: the rate is the city's; if the sale price was recorded wrongly,
/// correct the sale, and the tax follows.
law transfer-tax
  on gain
  when from is property | home
  // verify: the three rates against the Assessor-Recorder's current table.
  let rate = if proceeds <= 250_000 USD then 0.5% else if proceeds < 1_000_000 USD then 0.68% else 0.75%
  owe rate * proceeds to sf as transfer-tax
